val9=In \(\RR^3) with its usual scalar product denoted	\(< . , . >) let \(F) be the vector space spanned by ($val7) and ($val8).
val10=Find an orthogonal basis in \(F) formed by vectors	 \(v_1), \(v_2) with integral coefficients.	 Find a basis \(v_3) (with integral coefficients) of the orthogonal complement \(F^\perp) of \(F) .	 
tmp=!trim for	  Compute the norms of the three vectors you found	  First vector	  Second vector	  Direction vector \(v_3) of the orthogonal complement	  Norm of	  The two vectors form an independant system	  belongs to	  \(v_1) and \(v_2) form an orthogonal basis	  The vector \(v_3) is non-zero and belongs to the orthogonal of \(F)
val11=!translate internal $	\
$ to ;; in $tmp
!endif
